$DATUM 68-12-2
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Syntheses of Thioether Ligands.17 A reaction mixture containing
2‐hydroxythiophenol (7.92 mmol) in 8 mL of dry DMF was treated with KHCO3
(9.04 mmol) and bromide (7.92 mmol). The reaction mixture was stirred at
room temperature in the required time. The mixture was diluted with
water, then extracted with Et2O (3×20 mL). The combined organic phases
were washed with water, dried with MgSO4, filtered, and concentrated in
vacuo. Chromatography on silica gel (EtOAc/hexane, 3:97) give a colorless
oil. 2-(Ethylthio)phenol (HL-Et). Yield 85% (reaction in 0.5 h). ESIMS:
m/z = 153 [M-H]-; 1H NMR (300.1 MHz, CDCl3): δ 7.46 (d, 1H), 7.26 (t,
1H), 6.99 (d, 1H), 6.87 (t, 1H), 6.77 (s, 1H), 2.43 (q, 2H), 1.24 (d,
3H).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
